**Corollary 8.2 (individual four-expression requirement).** Any one acquired
spatial, chronological, boundary or callable-memory expression sufficient for a
task retaining these structural distinctions must acquire or lawfully access
them subject to the corresponding bounds above. Mutual recovery among four
expressions plus task sufficiency does not prove individual task minimality.

Proof. Restriction of a sufficient expression to the bracket family must separate
every literal-task class, by Proposition 8.1; local completion on the balanced
fiber must satisfy Theorem 7.3. For the second assertion reuse Process Geometry
43.1: mutual recoveries give a common kernel $N$ and sufficiency gives only
$N\subseteq K_{\mathcal V}$. Exactness additionally requires
$K_{\mathcal V}\subseteq N$, the no-redundancy direction. Four renamed copies
of full histories or numerically equal coordinates do not supply this condition
or a natural four-expression construction.

